    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0202" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg110"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Bridgman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your unnumbered dispatch
                    written at Keene, N. H., August 16, last, I have to say that you press again,
                    and urgently, for the prompt trial or discharge of Capt. John S. Bowles, who was
                    arrested October 4, 1894.</p>
                <p>You will report the result of your action to the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
